        <body>
            <div xml:id="d267">

                <pb facs="0350" n="246" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg246"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/4034: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai (Cunningham) to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-02-07T11:00:00+08:00">February 7, 1932—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 7—6 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>10. Mayor’s representative informed me today that it had been decided to use
                    Chinese aeroplanes against the Japanese, but he assured <pb facs="0351" n="247"
                        xml:id="pg247"/> me that Chinese aeroplanes would not carry bombs and would
                    take every precaution to prevent endangering the Settlement.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Legation, Nanking and Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cunningham</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
